From 7357311782ac8eb1b76b70b1ca6fbb5f20fd155c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 14:58:37 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Material: arrays synchronized on the host before each access
 on the host

The copies of the arrays of the materials on the host are made valid
before each access by mfem-mgis on the host:

- integration of the behaviours, update, revert, post-processings
  (`MultiMaterialNonLinearIntegrator::synchronizeOnHost`);
- accessors of the materials (`getGradient`, `getThermodynamicForce`,
  `getInternalStateVariable`, `getStoredEnergy`, `getDissipatedEnergy`):
  the mutable ones invalidate the copies on the device, the read-only
  ones keep them valid (`MaterialArrays::synchronizeOnHostForReading`).

`Material::synchronizeOnHost` is public, for the direct accesses to the
states. Without GPU device, nothing changes.

MaterialArraysTest: the accessors and the update of a problem see the
values written on the device (fails on the debug and cuda devices
without the synchronization in `update`).
